        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(msteams): cap team-group-id cache with pruneMapToMaxSize",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `teamGroupIdCache` Map in `resolveTeamGroupId` had TTL-based expiry (10 min) but no size cap. A large Teams workspace with many distinct team IDs could accumulate entries faster than the TTL window, allowing unbounded growth.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded a 500-entry cap via `pruneMapToMaxSize` — the shared SDK helper already used by 11 other files. The cap is applied after each successful cache insert.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo change for normal usage. Memory usage bounded at ~500 entries regardless of workspace size.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal-path proof — exercises the actual `resolveTeamGroupId` production code and `_teamGroupIdCacheForTest` with `tsx` (no VITEST guard):\n\n```text\n$ npx tsx proof-live.ts\n=== live-proof: resolveTeamGroupId cache bounded at 500 entries ===\n\n1. Cache hit team-0:             groupId = guid-0\n2. After 500 inserts:           cache.size = 500\n3. After 501st + prune:         cache.size = 500\n4. team-0 evicted (oldest):       true\n5. team-500 retained (newest):    true\n6. After 1000 inserts:          cache.size = 500\n7. team-999 retained (latest):    true\n8. Cache hit team-999:           groupId = guid-999\n\n=== PROOF COMPLETE ===\n```\n\n- Fills 500 entries through real cache object, verifies `resolveTeamGroupId` cache-hit path\n- 501st entry + prune: oldest evicted, cache stays at 500\n- 1000 total inserts: cache still at 500\n- `resolveTeamGroupId` cache-hit still returns correct groupId after pruning\n\nVitest — 27/27 passed including cache cap regression:\n\n```text\n$ vitest run --project extension-msteams extensions/msteams/src/graph-thread.test.ts\n\n ✓ resolveTeamGroupId > caps cache at 500 entries — evicts oldest on overflow\n ... 27 passed (27)\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
